n retries, and a new leader appends a new-term entry that can supply one.','No numeric deadline is specified; a finite absence alone cannot establish failure.'],unknowns=['Can a legal drained schedule enter a repeatable full protocol-state cycle after transfer failure while AutoLeave remains true?'],trigger_rationale='The public implicit-transition and tracker contracts assign departure to Raft when possible. The source names application as the retry trigger but the timeout clears only transfer state. A controlled drained schedule can distinguish a lost trigger from an independently scheduled retry; simple additional timer variants would not.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nclaim=dict(id='O-auto-joint-continuation',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For an implicit joint configuration assigned to Raft, after its entry has been applied and a transient leadership-transfer attempt has ended, a stable eligible leader with available joint quorums must retain an automatic path to propose leaving joint state. It must not remain in a closed repeating protocol execution with AutoLeave set and no leave proposal solely because the last application-triggered attempt was rejected during transfer.',source_ids=['S-joint-contract','S-joint-flag','S-applied'],scope=dict(description='Automatic continuation of implicit joint exit under a stable leader after failed transfer, with all emitted storage/application work completed and ordinary ticking/message delivery continued.',assumptions=['Non-Byzantine participants and valid initial configuration.','Synchronous caller persists before sends, applies entries/configurations before Advance, and processes all emitted work in order.','Transfer attempt may lose a TimeoutNow; after timeout the suffix delivers all network traffic and ticks every node.','No independent new client proposal or manual leave-joint is owed.'],excluded=['A fixed elapsed-time or tick deadline for leaving joint.','External client read completion or whole-cluster safety violation.','Schedules with missing application completion, unavailable quorum, leadership change or explicit joint mode.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S-applied','S-heartbeat-tick','S-abort','S-formation'],expectation_ids=['S-joint-contract','S-joint-flag'],binding_ids=['bind-auto-apply','bind-auto-abort'],derivation='ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit explicitly assigns automatic transition by a zero configuration proposal; Config.AutoLeave says Raft owns transition when possible. appliedTo initiates that proposal but the transfer guard may reject it. A closed repeatable healthy suffix with no emitted leave proposal would refute automatic continuation without inventing a deadline; finite noncompletion without recurrence would remain unknown.',applicability='Implicit joint mode with completion of the entering entry, transfer no longer active, and all ordinary protocol/application duties served.',unresolved=['The proposed recurrence observation must account for all behavior-determining state, queued messages, timers, callbacks and caller work.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Later client work or a leadership change could rescue the transition, but those are separate stimuli and are not used to define automatic continuation under the stable suffix.']))\nbind=[]\nfor id,mat,sym,a,b,desc in [('bind-auto-apply','S-applied','appliedTo',740,767,'Attempts zero-change proposal on eligible application completion and documents rejection during transfer.'),('bind-auto-abort','S-abort','abortLeaderTransfer',2057,2059,'Clears transfer state without scheduling the application-triggered continuation.')]:bind.append(dict(id=id,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=['S-joint-contract','S-joint-flag'],rationale='Links implementation continuation mechanism to the implicit-transition ownership contract.')]))\njson.dum